---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import GuideLayout from '../../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';

import shotCounsellor from '../../../assets/guide/11-student-counsellor.png';
---

<GuideLayout
  slug="student-privacy"
  title="What your school can and cannot see"
  description="Who reads your messages, who finds out you booked a session, and what your teachers are shown. Worth knowing before you start writing things down."
  audience="For students"
  readingTime="4 min read"
>
  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">1</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Your counsellor sees your side of Zengarden</h2>
      <p>
        The counsellor your school assigned to you can see the things you would expect the person
        supporting you to see:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, your email and your class.</li>
        <li>Messages between the two of you.</li>
        <li>Sessions you have booked with them.</li>
        <li>Any check-in or assessment they asked you to complete, and your answers.</li>
        <li>Concerns a teacher has raised about you, and what the teacher wrote.</li>
        <li>What you told the app when you set up your profile.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Only your counsellor.</strong> Other counsellors at your school cannot open your
        record. The system checks that you are actually assigned to someone before it shows them
        anything about you.
      </p>
      <figure>
        <Image
          src={shotCounsellor}
          alt="The My Counsellor page showing the one counsellor assigned to the student, with an Assigned badge."
          loading="eager"
        />
        <figcaption>
          One assigned counsellor, shown on your My Counsellor page. That is the person with access.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">2</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Your messages are encrypted</h2>
      <p>
        Messages between you and your counsellor are encrypted where they are stored. They are not
        sitting in a database as plain readable text that anyone poking around could scroll through.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-note">
        <p>
          <strong>Encrypted is not the same as secret from your counsellor.</strong> They can read
          your thread, because that is the point of it. What encryption stops is everyone else.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">3</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>What your teachers see, exactly</h2>
      <p>This is the part students usually want pinned down. A teacher of your class can see:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name on their class list.</li>
        <li>
          Whether there is an open referral about you, and what stage it is at. They see that a
          concern exists, not what is in it.
        </li>
        <li>
          The full text of a referral <strong>only if they wrote it themselves</strong>. A teacher
          cannot read a colleague's referral about you.
        </li>
        <li>
          A short closing summary when a case finishes, if your counsellor chooses to write one.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>A teacher cannot see:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your messages with your counsellor.</li>
        <li>Your counsellor's notes.</li>
        <li>Your answers to any assessment or check-in.</li>
        <li>That you booked a session, or when.</li>
        <li>Anything about students who are not in their own classes.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="guide-note guide-privacy">
        <p>
          <strong>If your own check-in flags that you are struggling</strong>, that goes to the
          counselling team and <strong>never appears to any teacher</strong>. It does not show on
          the class list and it is not in any teacher's referral list. Your own result stays between
          you and your counsellor.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">4</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>The resource library is not monitored</h2>
      <p>
        Guided exercises, articles and short courses are yours to use. Nobody is sent a report
        because you opened a breathing exercise at midnight or read the same article four times.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your counsellor can see assessments <strong>they assigned you</strong>. Material you browse
        on your own is not part of that.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">5</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>When your counsellor may involve someone else</h2>
      <p>
        Counselling is confidential, but it is not absolute, and you should know where the line sits
        before you need it rather than after.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your counsellor believes you or someone else is at serious risk of harm, they can take it
        to your school so your parents or guardians can be involved. When that happens they pass on
        what the school needs in order to act. Their session notes do not travel with it.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-note">
        <p>
          <strong>A good counsellor will tell you</strong> when they think something needs to go
          further, and why. If you are worried about this, ask them directly at the start of a
          session what would and would not stay between you. It is a completely reasonable question
          and they will have a clear answer.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">6</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Your data and your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Your school decides who is on its counselling team and which counsellor is assigned to your
        class. Zengarden stores the information above so that support can work.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want to know what is held about you, or you want it corrected or removed, ask your
        school first, since they run the account. You can also email
        <a href="mailto:admin@zengarden.co.in">admin@zengarden.co.in</a> directly.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our full <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> covers how information is handled and
        who it is shared with.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-footer">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Your counsellor sees your support.</strong> Your teachers see that a concern exists
      and nothing of its content unless they raised it themselves. Your own check-in results are
      never shown to teachers. Your messages are encrypted. Browsing the resource library is not
      tracked back to you.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>The exception is serious risk of harm</strong>, where your counsellor can involve your
      school and your family.
    </p>
    <p>
      Anything here unclear? Email <a href="mailto:admin@zengarden.co.in">admin@zengarden.co.in</a>
      and we will answer plainly.
    </p>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
